{"name":"Cats and Dogs","hex":"#8ea5b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cats and dogs","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy rain; a large amount of rain.","People or things that constantly fight (see fight like cats and dogs)."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Heavily; copiously; a lot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cats_and_dogs"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cats and Dogs (1932 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cats and Dogs is a 1932 short animated film and the fifth Pooch the Pup cartoon."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cats_and_Dogs_(1932_film)"},{"title":"Cats and Dogs (1952 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cats and Dogs is a 1952 Italian comedy film directed by Leonardo De Mitri and starring Titina De Filippo, Umberto Spadaro and Antonella Lualdi. The film's sets were designed by the art director Franco Lolli."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/ec/Cani_e_gatti_poster.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cats_and_Dogs_(1952_film)"},{"title":"Cats and Dogs (Warhol)","blocks":[{"text":"Cats and Dogs is a 1976 series of silkscreen paintings by American artist Andy Warhol. The set depicts stylized images of domestic cats and dog breeds. Produced during a period when Warhol increasingly embraced commissioned portraiture and decorative subject matter, the series reflects his interest in animals and the commercialization of imagery applied to familiar, intimate subjects."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cats_and_Dogs_(Warhol)"},{"title":"Cat","blocks":[{"text":"The cat, also called domestic cat and house cat, is a small domesticated carnivorous mammal. It is a member of Felidae, the family of mammals in the order Carnivora also colloquially referred to as cats. An obligate carnivore requiring a predominantly meat-based diet, it has retractable claws adapted to killing small prey species such as mice and rats. It has a strong, flexible body, quick reflexes, and sharp teeth, and its night vision and sense of smell are well developed. It is a social species, but a solitary hunter and a crepuscular predator.\nCat communication includes meowing, purring, trilling, hissing, growling, grunting, body language, and scent marking. It can hear sounds too faint or too high in frequency for human ears, such as those made by small mammals. It secretes and perceives pheromones. Cat intelligence is evident in its ability to adapt, learn through observation, and solve problems. The domestic cat is the only domesticated species of the family Felidae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Siam_lilacpoint.jpg/330px-Siam_lilacpoint.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cat"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Andy_Warhol_by_Jack_Mitchell.jpg/500px-Andy_Warhol_by_Jack_Mitchell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Andy_Warhol_by_Jack_Mitchell.jpg/500px-Andy_Warhol_by_Jack_Mitchell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Andy Warhol with his pet dachshund Archie, 1973","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAndy_Warhol_by_Jack_Mitchell.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Sheba1.JPG/500px-Sheba1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Sheba1.JPG/500px-Sheba1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASheba1.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Cat_August_2010-4.jpg/500px-Cat_August_2010-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&u